     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">Hi -- there isn&#39;t, but you can write a for-loop and loop through the tables and pull out the events for any specific node/branch.</span><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">The function &quot;prt&quot; will be helpful to see how the phylogeny is translated into a tree table data.frame.</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Cheers,</div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Nick</div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
